  "description": "01 §4.4 played out instead of asserted: enough power, too thin a corridor. An LV line of 150 MW runs from Modrzyca to Jasienica through a junction station at (7,6) — the station itself limits nothing (0.21), the line does. Jasienica connects on turn 14 and its 274–626 MW demand can only be served through that corridor: delivery pins at 166–197 MW (the line plus Modrzyca's own supply) and ENS runs 121–430 MW per turn. Day 3 wires in the second CCGT (500 MW) — offered power grows, delivery does not move, and the surplus setpoints turn into 332–398 MW of dump: more generation does not fix a corridor. The raise to MV ordered on the same turn lands during turn 30 — delivery jumps to 545 MW and ENS collapses to 0–62 MW.",
